{"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Grafluent"}],"title":"Extensions to Forest"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Trees","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions"],"anchor":"Trees"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"ShortestPaths","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:)"],"anchor":"ShortestPaths"},{"title":"SpanningTrees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:in:)"],"anchor":"SpanningTrees"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-forest-extensions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Forest-Extensions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","title":"Arborescence","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_arborescence"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Edmonds). A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"text":" are the children, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic, high-performance graph library for Swift."}],"title":"Grafluent","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Forest":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest","title":"Forest","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Forest","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A forest: an acyclic undirected graph, possibly empty, so a disjoint union of trees (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree). ","type":"text"},{"code":"trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists them by least vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"component(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says which one a vertex is in.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Forest","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Tree-Extensions":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Extensions to Tree","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-tree-extensions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/Trees/Forest/init(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/trees\/forest\/init(_:)","title":"init(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"The shortest-path forest of a search from any number of sources, with the edges’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directions and the roots dropped: every reached vertex, in the tree’s index order as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists them (unreached ones left out), and one edge (parent, child) per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached vertex with a parent, in that order. Edge positions are the forest’s own: edge k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"joins the k-th listed vertex with a parent to its parent; the graph’s edge stays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The tree holds a copy of its graph, so none is passed, unlike","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Forest(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a spanning forest. O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forest’s lookup table, unless they are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Tree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/Trees/Forest/init(_:in:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/trees\/forest\/init(_:in:)","title":"init(_:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spanning forest as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Forest"},{"type":"text","text":" of the graph it came from: every vertex of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph"},{"type":"text","text":", in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (an isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree), and the forest’s edges, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forest.edges"},{"type":"text","text":" order, each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.edges"},{"type":"text","text":" holds it. The edge at position k is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.edges[forest.edges[k]]"},{"type":"text","text":". SpanningForest keeps no copy of the graph, so it is passed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here; NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimum_spanning_tree"},{"type":"text","text":" returns this graph directly. O(n) expected: each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex and each edge end is hashed once, unless the vertices are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, when nothing is."}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-rootedtree-extensions","title":"Extensions to RootedTree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Extensions":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/extensions","title":"Extensions Across Modules","abstract":[{"text":"The members each module adds to types declared in another module, by extended type.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/RootedTree":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","title":"RootedTree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree with a root: an undirected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"depth(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preorder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Extensions to Arborescence","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-arborescence-extensions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions"}}}